Thousands of people gathered under the statue of Samoura Machela, Mozambique's founder's president in central Maputo, to shout peaceful slogans at a rare public demonstration.
“We want peace back; we want stability,” said Vanessa de Sousa, executive director of an investment firm.
For fear for her country's future, she exchanged corporate attire for a t-shirt decorated with the inscription "require security" in Portuguese and joined the crowd of Independence Square in the capital on Thursday.
