Jenny Slate was a member of the “Saturday night live” program and “Parks and Remediation”, but she became most famous for the fast-spreading series of “Marcel the shell with shoes”.
Both Kroll and Slate, as well as other young comedian with clearly recognizable voices (urreal pessimistic Anthony Jeselnik, salguous, racially oriented W. Kamau Bell), are the product of a decentralized world of American comedy.
One of the festival's biggest draws will be an interview: David Steinberg will speak to Larry David.
Steinberg began as a solo comedian, but he became a successful television and film director as well as an unofficial comedy historian.
From 2005 to 2007, he hosted a show called “Sit down comedy with David Steinberg”.
The reunion takes place at the Town Hall in downtown Manhattan.
"This city is definitely in the comedic DNA of Larry," Steinberg said.
