The number of people infected with HIV has surpassed a Thousand
In the Czech Republic, the number of infections is growing every year.
For example, in 2002 tests confirmed the infection in 50 people, five years later there were already 121, and in 2010 there were already 180.
Last year there were 212 infected and it was a record number.
"I don't think there is no doubt that the total number of newly diagnosed cases will surpass 200 this year," said Miroslav Hlavatý, an expert on the issue of AIDS, who for years led the Prague House of Light for patients.
There were 165 patients with HIV in the country last year from January to September, this year there were 176 in the same period.
Excluding monitoring to the end of this year’s September, the tests confirmed HIV in 1710 men and 353 women, most of whom were infected in Prague.
Their number reached 1005 in September.
In the Central Bohemian Region, 206 of those infected had residency.
Diagnosis was also listened to by 156 people from the South-Moravian region, 130 from the Moravian-Silesian and 116 from Ústí nad Labem.
Fewer of those infected come from the Vysočina region, there were 19.
A total of 88 per cent of patients became infected with sex.
In the past, fourteen people have become infected with blood transfusions.
However, such a case did not appear in the Czech Republic since the beginning of testing, i.e. for more than a quarter of a century.
Six children were also born with HIV, transferred from their mother.
