Physicians in Prague have already registered more than a thousand people with HIV.
From the onslior began in 1986 until the end of this year's third-degree tests confirmed the infection in a total of 1005 people from the metropolis.
This is according to the statistics of the National Reference Laboratory for AIDS of the State Health Institute.
According to her, there have been 2 063 infections so far throughout the Czech Republic.
In 396 the immune deficiency has already evaporated.
198 people have died.
The number of infections in the Czech Republic has been increasing every year in the last decade.
In 2002, the tests confirmed an infection in 50 people, five years later there were 121.
In 2009, 156 new infections were detected, and in 2010 180.
The number fell to 153 last year, on the contrary, last year it was record-breaking last year.
According to the laboratory, there were 212.
"I don't think there is a doubt that the total number of newly diagnosed cases will exceed 200 this year," says Miroslav Hlavatý, an expert on the issue of AIDS, who for years led the Prague House of Light for patients.
From October to the end of the year in 2011, tests revealed the outbreak in 39 people and last year in 47, Hlavatý said.
In September, the doctors registered 21 new patients and three patients.
