How Tipsport (doesn't) delete personal data.
More than a year a year ago, I made a registration on Tipsport.cz.
However, I didn’t finish it, because there was someone who couldn’t finish registering from the internet.
And because I did not want to go to another branch, the registration collapsed, then I switched and thanks to that I changed the address and the number of the identity card.
When I wanted to complete the registration later, I was told I couldn't, because I have a different OP number, an address and that I just can't complete it and that I should apply for the deletion of the data and make a new registration.
So I have done this and 24.10.2013 I wrote for technical support that I am requesting the deletion of all my personal data from the database according to a valid Personal Data Protection Act.
On this second day the technical support was written to me that I have to complete the registration at the branch.
In doing so, he started the marathon of e-mails for technical support, where they finally wrote that they deleted the personal data at my request.
Therefore, one would think that you could make the new registration and here the problems started again again at first it told me that my user name is already occupied (understood has not been erased - it is not a personal data, but in the end they also disqualified this).
So I used a different user name and it popped up that my personal data is already stored in order to complete the registration at the branch (how can they have stored something that they claim to be erased?), so I contacted technical support again.
When asked how it is possible, they wrote to me that they actually delebored the personal data on 25.10. and to send an e-mail with that error.
That's what I've done (Yesterday around 15 o'clock) and they wrote to me today that I registered the same day (31.10.2013) at 13.22 and that that's why I couldn't, because I used the same name and date of birth.
What I've been contacting technical support for a week and I'm figuring out that I still can't.
And what about the fact that if it were true what he claims (as it is not) could not be registered with the same name or the same date of birth if it has already been registered.
Just by the way, at those 13.22, I actually registered on the same name and the date of birth, but I used an imaginary e-mail and a phone number and world wonder, it appeared a page that I was emailed a link to complete the registration.
However, how is it possible if it is not possible to register on the same name and date of birth?
Probably because Tipsport binds e-mail registration and phone number and simply didn't disable the data as he claims.
So I once again communicated this to technical support that they simply lie (either intentionally or they don't know what they're saying), because what they're writing isn't true.
I've documented a few screenshots that the problem with registration was even before 31.10. so "fake" registration simply doesn't have an impact on this.
Tipsport wrote me a terrified sentence - I'm sorry, but because you're re-registered, we can't verify your claim.
And he ended communication.
Respectively, it repeats the same sentence that the registration binds to the name and date of birth.
They can't even accept the fact that the registration wasn't completed by clicking on that link in an e-mail and it didn't actually take place.
Therefore, if I sum it up, Tipsport not only hasn't erased data as he claims, but he's still lied when he claims otherwise.
Worse, it is possible to easily prove how they are lying and trying to make it look like the flaw is on the customer's side.
Incidentally, after the introduction of this matter on my personal blog, things started to move a little bit, and from Technical support came an e--mail that they are handing the matter forward for verification and I will be informed (after a week of urgency and arguing and accumulating about the same error).
