Jana Pét'ová: A step backwards.
So I decided to take a step backwards, but when I think about it, it's actually not a step at all, it's a big leap - a jump a few years back, to my memories to my childhood.
It's a remembrance of what it's been like not to have any worries and just come out of the school and wash the utensils, vacuum and do their homework.
Although these "obligations", it was mostly a theory, the wishes of the parents.
The practice was completely different - to run away from the school, throw the bag in the corner and run out.
To play with the rest of the children the ball games, to jump a dummy.
Then during the series Helen and her boys embroider ceremonial tablecloth for her grandmother for her birthday.
And then, after several warnings, to finally wash the utensils, vacuum, in the winter to carry wood into tiled stoves and do tasks after dark under the lamp (or to rely on a classmate and instead of tasks to write love verses addressed to school love).
In the morning to have breakfast of homemade strawberry marmelad (from a real fruit, not those jams that are sold now, the contents of which did not even lie next to the strawberries) and drank the tea from the dried herbs, which my mom and I so liked to collect.
I also remember those magical evenings when there was a tremble silence in the room, when my sister and I were recording songs from the radio on cassettes, which revolved loudly in an old cassette car from my mom.
And then we re-routed those cassettes and played the same song over and over and over again, our favorite, and they toasted a siphon with a siphon.
Or we were on the phone across the table using cans that were tied to each other with a string - and while we're at the phone call, to hear each other better, it was necessary to thoroughly brush your ears, the then crockery there was a match + cotton wool.
The minimum wage was more than three times lower than it is now, and my parents have been able to live that we didn't miss anything.
We didn't need any iPhones, iPads or even mobile phones and laptops or designer clothes.
Appaendages were inherited from generation to generation, and the best "necture" in the wardrobe was a batik T-shirt of homemade with the help of SAVA.
From the electronics it was enough for us to the satisfaction of the aforementioned mom's cassette player and maximally Walkman, which we shared with my sister and, by the way, we still used only on the train on a school trip.
We found it more interesting for us to play with Aunt Klobíček Hop or Man, don't be angry, or as I've already said go "only" out.
When I was a little older we got a video player under the tree, my parents certainly saved for him for a very long time, but unfortunately he didn't warm up with us for a long time.
My younger snurrel pungowed his strudel into him, she said he was going so beautifully the cassettes, so she tried to see if she was going to sleep the strudel as well.
I'm afraid he slept, but it was his last bite.
Well, he still has this incident, poor, on his dad's plate all the time.
She says that when Lenka was a little girl, she piled the strudel into the video and she thought she was going to replay the recipe and didn't play it, that's why she still couldn't bake it.
Remembrance how we were all able to communicate with each other, to communicate without a mobile phone, a computer.
My sister and I made an agreement with our neighbor's granddaughter on the holidays at our granddaughter, when we will meet again next summer with my grandparents - and that's how it was, that's how it was true.
We've come together.
Promise yourself with someone to see each other in a year's time?!
I also remember the winter, when the whole village and I were running outdoors, building snowmen, rode on a snow-sweating hill by the church on sacks stuffed with hay.
Then we died together with the whole family and talked about the past day.
Of course, my sister and I used to hear the notorious sentence before each supper: "Should wash your hands!"
Yes, the same is true even today, but I'm sure you don't have soap tied to the faucet in a lemon mesh.
After supper, when my father "worked" in the garage with Jarda from the village, my mom and I lay down on the floor, leaned our legs against a tiled stove, opened the door and stared at the flame and listened to the rupture of the wood, which flowed from the stove.
We've been closer - really - we didn't count how many friends we had on the social network, we knew how many friends we had, the real ones!
We communicated together - we talked - we didn't write messages every day through various chats, text messages.
There was no such thing, and yet we knew a lot more about each other.
I could go on like this for a long time.
It's lovely to remember, especially if I'm going to replenish these memories by reviewing albums where they're neatly glued with the black-and-white nudes.
And if I didn’t happen to know how much I was at that time, there is always a year of taking a picture from the back of the photo.
I'm looking at the fact that even though the haircuts didn't suit us very well according to the pot and we also had our pants two numbers bigger, no one laughed at us before, it was so normal (not IN).
And I'd rather go back a step forward - into reality.
Until 2013 and I will wait to see what the modern era will come up with maybe one day for my children.
What I don't know is that these remembrances of mine are now for the young teenage generation so at least somewhere "a hundred years behind monkeys" and I don't think they're losing a lot, that they won't experience this "pre-monster" time either.
I'd wish it on them!
The companies Google, Samsung and Huawei sued over Nortel patents
A group that owns thousands of patents of the defunct Nortel filed a lawsuit on Thursday in violating a patent against mobile phone makers, including Google, a company it relied on auction under Nortel bankrupt.
Consortium Rockstar, which purchased Nortel's $4.5-billion-$4.5-billion-dollar responsibility, has sued Samsung Electronics, HTC, Huawei, and four other companies for violating U.S. law enforcement in Texas.
Rockstar is jointly relied by Apple, Microsoft, Blackberry, Ericsson and Sony.
Google is accused of violating seven patents.
Appliions include technology that helps to combine Internet-visit-visited expressions with relevant ad, the lawsuit puts, a kernel for Google's search business.
Representatives of Samsung, Huawei, HTC and Rockstar were unavailable.
Samsung, Huawei and HTC produce phones that work on the Google Android operating system, which strongly competes with mobile products from Apple and Microsoft.
In 2011, Google made an initial bid of $900 million for Nortel patents.
Google has increased its offer several times, eventually offering up to $4.4 billion.
After being defeated by Rockstar in Nortel’s patent battle, Motorola Mobility gained $1.2.5 billion, a store motivated partly by Motorola’s patent groups.
“Despite the setback in an attempt to obtain patents under the case at auction, Google has infringed and continues to violating the patents,” the lawsuit said.
Rockstar seeks increased damages from Google because Google says there is a violation of the patent by Google intentionally, as the lawsuit claims.
