Václav Matyáš, President of the Association of Building Entrepreneurants in the Czech Republic: New Green Savings Should Continue
Since 2008, the Czech construction industry has struggled with a continuous decrease in the volume of contracts and the distaste of the state to deal with the issue of investment construction.
Announcement of the New Green Savings program was a positive signal for our construction industry, especially for small and medium-sized companies in individual regions.
It is a great opportunity not only for citizens, who, after the implementation of the measure, will save considerable amounts for heating, but also a chance for construction companies and manufacturers of building materials.
Each invest-invested billion will deliver more than 27,700 re-established vacancies to the state.
From the point of view of the fiscal policy of the state there are significant lever and multiplier effects, it is also one of the most significant pro-growth measures.
The Confederation of Building Entrepreneur companies in the Czech Republic therefore fundamentally disagrees with the resolution of the government and asks to implement such steps, which would allow further continuation of the program, so that further calls can be announced within it.
